msgid "prebattle/mission/text/1"
msgstr ""
"Brooks: \"So how are you? Have you come 'round? You'll see the medics later. Every gun counts now. The assault has already begun. And because we were late, the enemy's focused all their attention on another flank. This is our chance. We attack pronto. Break into town and squeeze them from both sides.\n"
"\n"
"Follow us — and avoid the dragon's teeth. They've got a bunch of rows of those concrete fangs in that field. But that's okay. We'll come through. All you gotta do is listen to me and execute my orders quickly and precisely. MacLeod and I will cover you.\n"
"\n"
"And don't pay his jokes any mind. Everyone has their own unique coping mechanisms… Forward!\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/1002"
msgstr ""
"Captain Smith: \"Listen up. Germany signed the surrender papers hours ago. The war ends tomorrow. But our boys in the mountains lost radio contact—they don't know it's over. They're set to attack this bloody fortress at dawn, and the Germans inside don't know about the surrender either. It'll be a pointless slaughter. \n"
"\n"
"We're the only ones who can stop it. Our mission: Sneak through enemy lines and deliver the ceasefire order. It's a suicide run, but every life we save is worth it. \n"
"\n"
"We've got a captured German radioman with us—he knows the terrain and he's got as much reason as we do to stop this bloodshed. \n"
"\n"
"Roll out.\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/1003"
msgstr ""
"Captain Dubois: \"The entire frontline is mined. We can't get through to our forces.\"\n"
"\n"
"Gefreiter Keller: \"These marks also show command posts. They have fragments of the passage map. For our...German scouts. We should look there.\"\n"
"\n"
"Captain Smith: \"So we're collecting map pieces. Let's move.\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/1004"
msgstr ""
"Captain Murphy: \"Man, what a maze! I would call it the MINE-otaur's labyrinth! Haha. Get it? No? Come on, that was gold!\"\n"
"\n"
"Captain Dubois: \"Just sneak through the minefield and I can finally get some...peace and quiet.\"\n"
"\n"
"Murphy: \"Tired of loading shells, Dubois?\"\n"
"\n"
"Dubois: \"That too.\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/1005"
msgstr ""
"Leni Scharf: \"The situation is critical. We've lost contact with our missile base in the Norwegian Sea. The reconnaissance flight never returned, and the initial tank landing force was wiped out by an unknown enemy.\n"
"\n"
"Intelligence suggests they're preparing to launch a ballistic missile. We don't know the target, but in this political climate, a single launch could trigger a global conflict.\n"
"\n"
"Feels like the old days, doesn't it? Just another impossible mission behind enemy lines. Roll out!\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/1006"
msgstr ""
"Leni Scharf: \"The situation is critical. We've lost contact with our missile base in the Norwegian Sea. The reconnaissance flight never returned, and the initial tank landing force was wiped out by an unknown enemy.\n"
"\n"
"Intelligence suggests they're preparing to launch a ballistic missile. We don't know the target, but in this political climate, a single launch could trigger a global conflict.\n"
"\n"
"Feels like the old days, doesn't it? Just another impossible mission behind enemy lines. Roll out!\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/2"
msgstr ""
"MacLeod: \"Ah, Tigers — those are the worst ye can face on the battlefield. And if the command says they have a problem, they probably mean Tigers. We cannot contact the first assault squad, the second's just departed, and here we are — sent to follow them.\n"
"\n"
"And if they send us, this can mean only one thing: Tigers. That's what they say at HQ: \"Send in those Tiger experts!\" Nine tanks for two. Not too shabby for half a year. Ye lead 5-4. But I've got a chance to get ahead. And finally get that damned medal!\n"
"\n"
"Come on — Brooks doesn’t like waiting. Our hunt begins.\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/3"
msgstr ""
"MacLeod: \"Alright, everyone, it's Operation Hammer and Anvil. Simple name "
"for a not-so-simple job. We're heading into the city to clear out enemy "
"forces. Won't be a walk in the park—we're up against some heavy armor. But "
"we've got brains, brawn, and teamwork on our side, right Lucky? And let's "
"make it snappy, folks. I've got plans with a wee cup of 'tea' at five, if "
"you get my drift!\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/4"
msgstr ""
"MacLeod: \"Don't ask, Lucky. I'm in the dark as much as you are.\n"
"\n"
"I'm not a fan of all this secrecy. I like things straightforward. You see the enemy, you fight. But this? It's a mess.\n"
"\n"
"There'll be allied tanks in the city too. Brooks asked us to tread carefully. What's that supposed to mean?\n"
"We've got a special job. To find some sort of Wunderwaffe—something huge on tracks. No one else to do it but us, Lucky.\n"
"\n"
"Ready? Let's roll.\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/5"
msgstr ""
"Captain John McCormick: \"Alright, fellas, the day has come. It's time to put an end to this war, and that's exactly what we're gonna do. All of us, together–Americans, Brits, French, Canadians, Australians, Belgians, Czechoslovaks, Greeks, Dutch, Kiwis, Norwegians, Poles. We're united to put an end to this evil once and for all.\n"
"\n"
"We're gonna break through the Atlantic Wall and establish our foothold.\n"
"\n"
"Get ready for the landing!\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/6"
msgstr ""
"Captain Smith: \"Listen up. Germany signed the surrender papers hours ago. The war ends tomorrow. But our boys in the mountains lost radio contact—they don't know it's over. They're set to attack this bloody fortress at dawn, and the Germans inside don't know about the surrender either. It'll be a pointless slaughter. \n"
"\n"
"We're the only ones who can stop it. Our mission: Sneak through enemy lines and deliver the ceasefire order. It's a suicide run, but every life we save is worth it. \n"
"\n"
"We've got a captured German radioman with us—he knows the terrain and he's got as much reason as we do to stop this bloodshed. \n"
"\n"
"Roll out.\""

msgid "prebattle/mission/text/7"
msgstr ""
"Leni Scharf: \"The situation is critical. We've lost contact with our missile base in the Norwegian Sea. The reconnaissance flight never returned, and the initial tank landing force was wiped out by an unknown enemy.\n"
"\n"
"Intelligence suggests they're preparing to launch a ballistic missile. We don't know the target, but in this political climate, a single launch could trigger a global conflict.\n"
"\n"
"Feels like the old days, doesn't it? Just another impossible mission behind enemy lines. Roll out!\""

